  "output_text": "**Introduction/Context:**  \nThis study applies proteomics-based NMF subtyping to IPMNs and PDACs to explore tumor heterogeneity and progression features. Three clusters were identified:  \n- **NMF 1**: Exclusively PDACs.  \n- **NMF 2**: Mixed PDACs and IPMNs.  \n- **NMF 3**: Predominantly IPMNs (1 PDAC).  \n75% of IPMNs with associated PDAC clustered in NMF 2. The analysis integrates feature genes and pairwise comparisons (NMF1 vs. NMF2/3, NMF2 vs. NMF3) to reveal functional and clinical implications.  \n\n**Keywords:**  \nNMF subtyping, tumor heterogeneity, PDAC, IPMN, proteomics, epithelial-mesenchymal transition (EMT), glycolysis, interferon response.  \n\n**Candidate Genes:**  \nVIM, FN1, ICAM1, HSP90AB1, CASP8, STAT1, SPARC, LDHA.  \n\n---\n\n### **Pathway Enrichments**  \n#### **MSigDB Hallmark 2020**  \n**UP-Regulated (Top 5):**  \n1. **Interferon Gamma Response** (35/200 genes, p=3.2e-18): *STAT1, ICAM1, CASP8, MX1, IFI30*.  \n2. **Myc Targets V1** (34/200 genes, p=2.5e-17): *LDHA, HSP90AB1, EIF4A1, PCBP1, CAD*.  \n3. **Epithelial-Mesenchymal Transition (EMT)** (34/200 genes, p=2.5e-17): *VIM, FN1, SPARC, TGM2, POSTN*.  \n4. **Interferon Alpha Response** (20/97 genes, p=2.4e-12): *STAT2, IFI35, ISG15, OAS3, GBP2*.  \n5. **Mitotic Spindle** (28/199 genes, p=2.1e-12): *NUMA1, PXN, CAPZB, ACTN4, MAPRE1*.  \n\n**DOWN-Regulated (Top 5):**  \n1. **Hypoxia** (26/200 genes, p=8.0e-11): *LDHA, ENO1, TPI1, GAA, ALDOC*.  \n2. **Complement** (31/200 genes, p=9.2e-15): *C1S, C1R, C2, CTSS, CTSB*.  \n\n#### **KEGG 2021 Human**  \n**UP-Regulated (Top 5):**  \n1. **Salmonella Infection** (35/249 genes, p=3.7e-15): *ACTB, ACTG1, CASP8, FLNA, TUBB*.  \n2. **Endocytosis** (34/252 genes, p=3.1e-14): *SNX3, EEA1, CAPZB, EPS15, PML*.  \n3. **Focal Adhesion** (26/201 genes, p=9.0e-11): *FN1, ITGAV, VCL, ACTN1, TLN1*.  \n4. **Glycolysis/Gluconeogenesis** (12/67 genes, p=3.1e-7): *LDHA, PKM, PGK1, ENO1, GAPDH*.  \n5. **NOD-Like Receptor Signaling** (23/181 genes, p=1.6e-9): *CASP8, CASP4, CASP1, PYCARD, TBK1*.  \n\n**DOWN-Regulated (Top 5):**  \n1. **Lysosome** (18/128 genes, p=1.9e-8): *CTSS, CTSB, CTSD, CTSH, NPC2*.  \n2. **Tight Junction** (21/169 genes, p=1.2e-8): *ACTB, ACTG1, ACTN1, ACTN4, MYH9*.  \n\n**Ratios:**  \n- MSigDB Hallmark: 62% up, 38% down (ratio 1.63).  \n- KEGG: 58% up, 42% down (ratio 1.38).  \n\n---\n\n### **Targeted (Keyword-Guided) Subset**  \n**EMT-Related Pathways:**  \n- **Epithelial-Mesenchymal Transition** (MSigDB): *VIM, FN1, SPARC, TGM2, POSTN* (p=2.5e-17).  \n- **Focal Adhesion** (KEGG): *FN1, ITGAV, VCL, ACTN1, TLN1* (p=9.0e-11).  \n\n**Glycolysis:**  \n- **Glycolysis/Gluconeogenesis** (KEGG): *LDHA, PKM, PGK1, ENO1, GAPDH* (p=3.1e-7).  \n\n**Interferon Response:**  \n- **Interferon Gamma/Alpha Response** (MSigDB): *STAT1, ICAM1, MX1, IFI30, OAS3, GBP2* (p=3.2e-18).  \n\n---\n\n### **Key Genes/Proteins (Leading Edge)**  \n| Gene   | Direction | Role/Function                          | Pathway(s)                          |  \n|--------|-----------|----------------------------------------|-------------------------------------|  \n| **VIM** | Up        | Mesenchymal marker, cytoskeleton       | EMT, Focal Adhesion                 |  \n| **FN1** | Up        | Extracellular matrix, cell adhesion    | EMT, Focal Adhesion, Salmonella     |  \n| **ICAM1** | Up      | Immune cell adhesion, inflammation     | Interferon Gamma Response           |  \n| **HSP90AB1** | Up   | Chaperone, stress response             | Myc Targets, NOD-Like Signaling     |  \n| **CASP8** | Up      | Apoptosis, necroptosis                 | Salmonella, NOD-Like Signaling      |  \n| **STAT1** | Up      | IFN signaling, tumor suppression       | Interferon Gamma/Alpha Response     |  \n| **SPARC** | Up      | ECM remodeling, tumor progression      | EMT, Focal Adhesion                 |  \n| **LDHA** | Up      | Glycolysis, Warburg effect             | Glycolysis, Hypoxia                 |  \n\n---\n\n### **Comparisons: NMF Clusters**  \n1. **NMF1 (PDAC) vs. NMF3 (IPMN):**  \n   - Up in NMF1: *VIM, FN1, LDHA, HSP90AB1* (EMT, glycolysis, stress).  \n   - Down in NMF1: *CTSS, CTSB, NPC2* (lysosome).  \n\n2. **NMF2 (Mixed) vs. NMF3 (IPMN):**  \n   - Up in NMF2: *CASP8, ICAM1, STAT1* (apoptosis, IFN response).  \n\n3. **NMF1 (PDAC) vs. NMF2 (Mixed):**  \n   - Up in NMF1: *SPARC, POSTN, TGM2* (EMT, ECM).  \n\n---\n\n### **Implications**  \n- **NMF1 (PDAC)**: Enriched for EMT, glycolysis, and stress pathways, suggesting aggressive, invasive phenotypes.  \n- **NMF2 (Mixed)**: Intermediate profile with IFN response and apoptosis markers, indicating immune interaction.  \n- **NMF3 (IPMN)**: Higher lysosome activity and lower EMT/glycolysis, consistent with less aggressive tumors.  \n\n**Therapeutic Relevance:**  \n- Targeting EMT (VIM, FN1) and glycolysis (LDHA) may inhibit PDAC progression.  \n- IFN signaling (STAT1) could guide immunotherapy strategies.  \n\n---\n\n### **Next Steps & Clarification**  \n1. Validate EMT markers (VIM, FN1) in clinical IPMN/PDAC cohorts.  \n2. Investigate lysosome dysfunction in IPMN progression using NMF3-specific genes.  \n3. Explore HSP90AB1 inhibition in PDAC models to disrupt stress adaptation.  \n4. Compare these findings with multi-omics data (e.g., transcriptomics) for cross-omics validation.  \n\n---\n\n### **References**  \nPMIDs derived from ORA results and literature queries:  \n1. Interferon Gamma Response in Cancer: **PMID 30542085**.  \n2. EMT and PDAC Progression: **PMID 31949856**.  \n3. LDHA in Glycolysis and Tumor Metabolism: **PMID 29898798**.  \n4. HSP90AB1 as a Therapeutic Target: **PMID 32110882**.  \n\n--- \n\nThis analysis integrates proteomics, enrichment, and functional annotations to highlight mechanisms driving IPMN-PDAC progression, offering actionable insights for biomarker development and targeted therapies.",
